{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q411467","formula":"Cl₆H₂Pt","hill":"Cl6H2Pt","elements":["H","Cl","Pt"],"composition":{"H":2.0,"Cl":6.0,"Pt":1.0},"names":{"en":"Platinic chloride","ru":"Гексахлороплатинат(IV) водорода"},"descriptions":{"en":"Chloroplatinic acid (also known as hexachloroplatinic acid) is an inorganic compound with the formula [H3O]2[PtCl6](H2O)x (0 ≤ x ≤ 6). A red solid, it is an important commercial source of platinum, usually as an aqueous solution. Although often written in shorthand as H2PtCl6, it is the hydronium (H3O+) salt of the hexachloroplatinate anion (PtCl2−6).","ru":"Гексахлороплатинат(IV) водорода — неорганическое соединение, комплексное соединение металла платины с формулой H2[PtCl6], оранжево-жёлтые кристаллы, хорошо растворяется в воде, получен в виде кристаллогидрата."},"fame":25,"pubchemCid":61859,"mass":409.8,"charge":0,"smiles":"[H+].[H+].Cl[Pt-2](Cl)(Cl)(Cl)(Cl)Cl","inchikey":"GBFHNZZOZWQQPA-UHFFFAOYSA-J","iupac":"hexachloroplatinum(2-);hydron","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"61859","atoms":9,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.099,"y":-1.961,"z":-0.09,"el":"Cl"},{"x":0.1,"y":0.144,"z":0.19,"el":"Pt"},{"x":2.415,"y":0.865,"z":0.867,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-2.016,"y":-0.824,"z":0.004,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.431,"y":-1.391,"z":0.993,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-1.451,"y":1.938,"z":-0.103,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-1.304,"y":-0.752,"z":1.667,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.181,"y":1.885,"z":-1.242,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.256,"y":0.094,"z":-2.284,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1.0],[1,2,1.0],[1,3,1.0],[1,4,1.0],[1,5,1.0],[1,6,1.0]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q411467","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chloroplatinic_acid","license"